.TH PM_FINDGPSLOCK 1 "May 2026" "v1.9.10a" "CamClops - GPS Lock Finder"
.SH NAME
clops_findgpslock \- report GPS lock acquisition time for dashcam footage segments
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B clops_findgpslock
[\fB\-\-verbose\fR] \fIfile.ts\fR [\fIfile2.ts\fR \fI...\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B clops_findgpslock
scans one or more dashcam footage segments that carry a LIGOGPSINFO GPS stream
and reports when GPS lock was acquired relative to the start of each clip.
The Pruveeo D90 is the primary confirmed camera for this GPS format.
.PP
Cameras using the LIGO firmware GPS stream do not write GPS records
until a satellite fix is acquired.  The lock offset
.RB ( +Ns )
is computed by comparing the UTC timestamp of the first valid GPS record
against the local clip-start time encoded in the filename, using epoch
arithmetic for accuracy across midnight crossings and DST boundaries.
.PP
For each file,
.B clops_findgpslock
prints a header line with the filename and the clip-start time derived from
the filename, followed by the lock line showing the offset and the first
valid GPS fix.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-v ", " \-\-version
Print version information and exit.
.TP
.B \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Pass verbose flags to ExifTool and show its stderr output during the scan.
Useful for diagnosing extraction failures.
.SH OUTPUT
.nf
# 20260216_095422F.ts  2026-02-16 09:54:22
  lock +107s  20260216 15:56:09    30.415534   -89.027873
.fi
.PP
The header line shows the filename and the clip-start time (local) derived
from the filename.  The lock line shows:
.TP
.B lock +Ns
Seconds elapsed from clip start until the first valid GPS fix.
.TP
.I timestamp
GPS lock time in UTC
.RB ( YYYYMMDD\ HH:MM:SS ).
.TP
.I lat\~\~lon
Latitude and longitude at the moment of lock, in decimal degrees.
.PP
If no valid GPS record is found in the file, the message
.B (no GPS lock found)
is printed instead.
.SH NOTES
Filename timestamps are in local time; GPS timestamps are in UTC.
The offset computation accounts for the timezone difference via
.BR mktime (3)
(local) and
.BR timegm (3)
(UTC).
.PP
A lock offset of
.B +0s
is theoretically possible on a warm-start trip where the receiver retained
its last fix.  In practice the D90 typically shows 20\(en120 seconds on a
cold start.
.PP
This tool is diagnostic.
.B gpsLockSeconds
is populated automatically in the trip manifest whenever GPS is extracted
.RB ( "camclops \-G" ,
.BR clops_gpsexport (1),
or the GUI GPS tab) and can be batch-populated with
.BR "clops_gpsinfo \-\-scan\-all\-trips" .
Lock times are surfaced in the interactive browser and
.BR clops_ls (1).
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
.B 0
At least one file processed without error.
.TP
.B 1
Bad arguments or file not found.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR camclops (1),
.BR clops_gpsinfo (1),
.BR clops_gpsexport (1),
.BR exiftool (1)
